# robot-feed.fk: the kit's robots back into a roboport. Plot 12x8. The kit's robots end up as
# items in a storage chest whenever a build takes up the roboport that held them; a requester asks
# for them and one inserter drops them into the roboport. Place it on free ground inside the
# network; `cover power` powers it.
# Run:  fk check robot-feed.fk    fk build
# Expect: `check robot-feed: 2 machines, 1 nets, 0 check lines`; `routed load: 1 -> 1, 1 inserter
# (direct insertion)`. A second chest with item="construction-robot" does the same for those.
port  = Roboport @(0, 0)
botin = Chest<requester, item="logistic-robot", request=50, rate=1/s> @(5, 1)
net load: botin -> port
